<https://w3id.org/ontodesire> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire/0.3.0> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire/commitments> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A reference ontology of desire that reifies rival philosophical theories of desire as first-class entities, keeping the Desire class deliberately underdetermined. Includes characteristic marks, objections, the four orthogonal partitions of desire, per-theory categorial stances, and bibliographic anchoring."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/desire/> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "OntoDesire"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "For declaring commitments only, import <https://w3id.org/ontodesire/commitments> alone."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "0.3.0" .
