<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#Desire> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "desire"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#Desire> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A conative mental state whose content specifies a satisfaction condition to be realized in the world. Deliberately underdetermined: the essential nature of desire is what the reified theories in this ontology disagree about."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#Desire> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#commitsToStructuralStance> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#SingleBearer> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#Desire> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#commitsToStructuralStance> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#StandingDesiresGenuine> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#Desire> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#commitsToStructuralStance> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#UniversalWorldToMindFit> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#Desire> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#deliberatelyUncommittedOn> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#FamilyAxis> .
_:genid11 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom> .
_:genid11 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#Desire> .
_:genid11 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#commitsToStructuralStance> .
_:genid11 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#SingleBearer> .
_:genid11 <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#commitmentEvidence> "Desire rdfs:subClassOf [ owl:onProperty hasBearer ; owl:cardinality 1 ] (this module, Section 12)." .
_:genid11 <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#commitmentNote> "Declared by OntoDesire itself. Excludes plural/shared subjects of one desire token; collective-conation theorists would contest it." .
_:genid12 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom> .
_:genid12 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#Desire> .
_:genid12 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#commitsToStructuralStance> .
_:genid12 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#StandingDesiresGenuine> .
_:genid12 <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#commitmentEvidence> "Desire owl:equivalentClass [ owl:unionOf ( OccurrentDesire StandingDesire ) ] (this module, Section 3.3)." .
_:genid12 <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#commitmentNote> "Declared by OntoDesire itself. Some dispositionalists deny that standing desires are genuine desires, reading them as mere dispositions to generate occurrent ones (see the skos:note on StandingDesire)." .
_:genid13 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom> .
_:genid13 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#Desire> .
_:genid13 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#commitsToStructuralStance> .
_:genid13 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#UniversalWorldToMindFit> .
_:genid13 <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#commitmentEvidence> "Desire rdfs:subClassOf [ owl:onProperty hasDirectionOfFit ; owl:hasValue WorldToMind ] (this module, Section 7). The axiom is universal, not exclusive: nothing caps hasDirectionOfFit, so a desire may consistently also bear mind-to-world fit." .
_:genid13 <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#commitmentNote> "Declared by OntoDesire itself. Retained deliberately: universal world-to-mind fit is the closest thing to common ground the debate has, but it is contested in the desire-as-belief debate that Lewis (1988) opened by attacking the thesis, by its contemporary defenders (Gregory 2021), and in the besire literature -- a commitment, not a neutral fact." .
_:genid14 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom> .
_:genid14 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#Desire> .
_:genid14 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#deliberatelyUncommittedOn> .
_:genid14 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#FamilyAxis> .
_:genid14 <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#commitmentEvidence> "skos:definition of Desire: 'Deliberately underdetermined: the essential nature of desire is what the reified theories in this ontology disagree about.'" .
_:genid14 <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#commitmentNote> "The flagship design decision in machine-readable form: the essence-level axis is deliberately uncommitted -- the rival theories are reified, not adjudicated." .
