# https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DesireAsBeliefInGood
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DesireAsBeliefInGood> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DesireAsBeliefInGood> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#MonofactorialTheory> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DesireAsBeliefInGood> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#attributedTo> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#Socrates> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DesireAsBeliefInGood> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#belongsToFamily> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#GoodBasedFamily> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#GoodBasedFamily> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DesireAsBeliefInGood> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#defendedBy> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#AlexGregory> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DesireAsBeliefInGood> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#identifiesDesireWith> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#GoodBeliefDisposition> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DesireAsBeliefInGood> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#impliesCategory> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DoxasticStateCategory> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DoxasticStateCategory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DesireAsBeliefInGood> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#suffersObjection> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#AnimalObjection> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DesireAsBeliefInGood> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#suffersObjection> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#LewisDecisionTheoreticObjection> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DesireAsBeliefInGood> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "desire as belief in the good"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DesireAsBeliefInGood> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "To desire p is to believe that p is good (or, in the contemporary variant, that one has normative reason to bring p about)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DesireAsBeliefInGood> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "The attribution to Socrates is a classical antecedent (the Socratic thesis that we desire the good), not a formulation of the analysis; the analysis is actively defended in the contemporary literature (Gregory, Desire as Belief, OUP 2021)."@en .
