<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#MentalProcessCategory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DirectedAttention> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#suffersObjection> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#NarrowAttentionObjection> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DirectedAttention> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "directed-attention theory"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DirectedAttention> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "To desire p is for the thought of p to keep occurring in a favourable light, with attention directed insistently toward considerations counting in favour of p."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DirectedAttention> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Technically a sufficient condition rather than a full theory; fits occurrent desires best."@en .
