<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#MotivatingGoodBeliefObjection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "motivating belief-in-good objection"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#MotivatingGoodBeliefObjection> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Judgments of what is good or obligatory also dispose to action; action-based theories fail to distinguish desire from goodness judgment."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/ontodesire#NarrowAttentionObjection
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#NarrowAttentionObjection> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#NarrowAttentionObjection> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#Objection> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#NarrowAttentionObjection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "narrow attentional focus objection"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#NarrowAttentionObjection> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Desire directs attention also to information about p, to opportunities to obtain it, and to those discussing p — not only to reasons in favour of p."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/ontodesire#Nora
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#Nora> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
