# 
# https://w3id.org/ontodesire#PleasureDisposition
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#PleasureDisposition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#PleasureDisposition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#CharacteristicMark> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#PleasureDisposition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "disposition to pleasure at its seeming that p, displeasure at its seeming that not-p"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#PleasureDisposition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Family-grain mark: the hedonic neural-identity theory reads it occurrently (desires ARE pleasure/reward episodes) rather than dispositionally, which is why the causal-priority objection targets only the dispositional variant. A dispositional/occurrent mark split, mirroring the good-based split, is a candidate refinement for the next version."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/ontodesire#PropositionsAsStatesOfAffairs
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#PropositionsAsStatesOfAffairs> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RationalityAcquisition
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RationalityAcquisition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RationalityAcquisition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#OriginMechanism> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RationalityAcquisition> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#defendedBy> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#MichaelSmith> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RationalityAcquisition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "acquisition via reasoning about one's rationality"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RationalityAcquisition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Believing that, were one rational, one would desire p tends to generate an intrinsic desire for p; breaks with the Humean dictum that beliefs do not dictate intrinsic desire."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RationalityAcquisition> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#generates> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#IntrinsicDesire> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/ontodesire#ReasonsAttention
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#ReasonsAttention> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#ReasonsAttention> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#CharacteristicMark> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#ReasonsAttention> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "disposition to have attention drawn to reasons in favour of p"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningDrive
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningDrive> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningDrive> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#CharacteristicMark> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningDrive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "use of representations of p to drive reward-based learning"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningTheory
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningTheory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningTheory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#MonofactorialTheory> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningTheory> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#anticipatedBy> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#FredDretske> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningTheory> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#belongsToFamily> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#LearningBasedFamily> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningTheory> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#defendedBy> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#TimothySchroeder> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningTheory> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#identifiesDesireWith> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningDrive> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningTheory> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#impliesCategory> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#LearningMechanismCategory> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningTheory> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#locatesDesireIn> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#DopaminergicRewardSystem> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningTheory> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#suffersObjection> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#AprioriImplausibilityObjection> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningTheory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "reward-learning theory"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningTheory> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "To desire p is to use representations of p to drive reward-based learning."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#RewardLearningTheory> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Treats desire as a natural kind; the least a priori credible of the listed theories."@en .
