# 
# https://w3id.org/ontodesire#norasStandingDesireForNewTeas
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#norasStandingDesireForNewTeas> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#norasStandingDesireForNewTeas> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#IntrinsicDesire> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#norasStandingDesireForNewTeas> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#StandingDesire> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#norasStandingDesireForNewTeas> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#hasBearer> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#Nora> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#norasStandingDesireForNewTeas> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#hasContent> <https://w3id.org/ontodesire#noraTriesNewTeas> .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#norasStandingDesireForNewTeas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Nora's standing desire to try new teas"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ontodesire#norasStandingDesireForNewTeas> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Example of the explanatory role of standing desires: explains why the new tin captures her attention and why she is delighted. No strength individual is asserted: under v0.3.0's max-1 axiom a desire need not carry a determinate cardinal strength."@en .
